[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# Rijksmuseum: EDM collection dump\n\nExplores the subset of the Rijksmuseum's [EDM collection dump](https://data.rijksmuseum.nl/docs/data-dumps/historical-dumps) (January 2020, all 668,000 published objects, metadata CC0) that the `rijksmuseum` step keeps: objects whose title or description names a village or mentions drowning, and objects that refer to a place or event named after a village or to a flood.\n\n**Before running:** run `pnpm --filter @verdronkendorpen/exploration run fetch:rijksmuseum`. It downloads the dump (153 MB zipped) once and writes the subset to `dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt`, which every cell uses as its endpoint. The whole dump (1.5 GB of Turtle) is too big to query here.\n\nThe data uses the Europeana Data Model: objects are `edm:ProvidedCHO` with Dublin Core fields, their image and licence sit on an `ore:Aggregation`, and places, events, concepts and people come from the Rijksmuseum thesaurus (`hdl.handle.net/10934/RM0001.THESAU.*`) with only a `skos:prefLabel`, and coordinates for some places.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Overview\n\nWhich classes occur, and how often.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?class (COUNT(?s) AS ?count) WHERE {\n  ?s a ?class\n}\nGROUP BY ?class\nORDER BY DESC(?count)",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Objects\n\nProperties used on the objects, and how many objects use each.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?property (COUNT(DISTINCT ?object) AS ?objects) WHERE {\n  ?object a edm:ProvidedCHO ;\n    ?property ?value .\n}\nGROUP BY ?property\nORDER BY DESC(?objects)",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Places\n\n`dc:subject` links an object to what it depicts, including places; `dct:spatial` links it to where it was made. The places most often depicted in the subset, with their coordinates where the thesaurus has them.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?place ?label ?lat ?long (COUNT(DISTINCT ?object) AS ?objects) WHERE {\n  ?object dc:subject ?place .\n  ?place a edm:Place ;\n    skos:prefLabel ?label .\n  OPTIONAL { ?place wgs84_pos:lat ?lat ; wgs84_pos:long ?long }\n}\nGROUP BY ?place ?label ?lat ?long\nORDER BY DESC(?objects)\nLIMIT 100",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "Production places (`dct:spatial`), mostly where a print was published.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?label (COUNT(DISTINCT ?object) AS ?objects) WHERE {\n  ?object dct:spatial ?place .\n  ?place skos:prefLabel ?label .\n}\nGROUP BY ?label\nORDER BY DESC(?objects)\nLIMIT 50",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Events\n\nEvents (`edm:TimeSpan`) the objects show, such as floods, sieges and battles, via `dc:subject` or `dct:temporal`.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?label (COUNT(DISTINCT ?object) AS ?objects) WHERE {\n  ?object dc:subject|dct:temporal ?event .\n  ?event a edm:TimeSpan ;\n    skos:prefLabel ?label .\n}\nGROUP BY ?label\nORDER BY DESC(?objects)",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Dates\n\n`dct:created` is free text, in Dutch and English: \"1696\", \"ca. 1700 - voor 1720\", \"1696-05-12\". The most common forms, with digits replaced by 9.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?form (COUNT(*) AS ?count) WHERE {\n  ?object dct:created ?created .\n  FILTER(LANGMATCHES(LANG(?created), \"nl\"))\n  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?created), \"[0-9]\", \"9\") AS ?form)\n}\nGROUP BY ?form\nORDER BY DESC(?count)\nLIMIT 30",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Images and licences\n\nThe aggregation holds the image (`edm:isShownBy`) and the rights of the image (`edm:rights`). The image links (Google-hosted) still worked in October 2026.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?rights (COUNT(?aggregation) AS ?objects) (SUM(IF(BOUND(?image), 1, 0)) AS ?withImage) WHERE {\n  ?aggregation a ore:Aggregation ;\n    edm:rights ?rights .\n  OPTIONAL { ?aggregation edm:isShownBy ?image }\n}\nGROUP BY ?rights\nORDER BY DESC(?objects)",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Invalid IRIs\n\nThe dump has a few hundred IRIs that aren't absolute (\"ttp://vocab.getty.edu/...\", \"Balmoral boots\"). The step rewrites them to `urn:invalid-iri:<encoded>` so the files parse. The ones left in the subset:",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?object ?property ?value WHERE {\n  ?object ?property ?value .\n  FILTER(isIRI(?value) && STRSTARTS(STR(?value), \"urn:invalid-iri:\"))\n}\nLIMIT 50",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Example: Reimerswaal\n\nObjects that depict Reimerswaal or name it in their title, with their date and image.",
    "metadata": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "sparql",
    "value": "# [endpoint=../../dumps/rijksmuseum-edm-subset.nt]\nPREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>\nPREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\nPREFIX edm: <http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/edm/>\nPREFIX ore: <http://www.openarchives.org/ore/terms/>\nPREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\nPREFIX wgs84_pos: <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#>\n\nSELECT ?object ?number ?title ?created ?image WHERE {\n  ?object a edm:ProvidedCHO ;\n    dc:identifier ?number ;\n    dc:title ?title .\n  {\n    ?object dc:subject/skos:prefLabel ?place .\n    FILTER(CONTAINS(?place, \"Reimerswaal\"))\n  } UNION {\n    FILTER(CONTAINS(?title, \"Reimerswaal\"))\n  }\n  OPTIONAL { ?object dct:created ?created . FILTER(LANGMATCHES(LANG(?created), \"nl\")) }\n  OPTIONAL { ?aggregation edm:aggregatedCHO ?object ; edm:isShownBy ?image }\n}\nORDER BY ?number",
    "metadata": {}
  }
]
